[Mandatory DNAM Branding & Format Integrity](#mandatory-dnam-branding--format-integrity).

## Mandatory DNAM Branding & Format Integrity

Your license to distribute, embed, or link any part of the software in any
hardware device, firmware, audio plugin, or software application is strictly
conditioned on all of the following:

1. **Mandatory User-Facing DNAM Branding (No White-Labeling):** Any hardware
   device, embedded firmware, closed-source or open-source audio plugin, or
   software application that links, embeds, or executes `dnam-engine` (or its
   bindings) or loads `.dnam` models must visibly identify and credit the
   modeling technology as **"DNAM"** ("Dynamic Neural Audio Modeler") or
   **"Powered by DNAM"** wherever the modeling engine, effect block/module, or
   model loader is presented to end users (including plugin GUI faceplates or
   headers, hardware screen block/module selectors, model/preset browsers,
   "About" views, and product documentation/specifications). You may not
   white-label, rebrand, obscure, or market `dnam-engine` or the DNAM modeling
   architecture under a substitute proprietary technology name.
2. **`.dnam` Container & Schema Integrity:** Any product or tool that loads,
   saves, generates, or exchanges DNAM models must preserve the unmodified
   `.dnam` and `.dnam-ckpt` file extensions and internal schema identifiers
   (`"architecture": "DNAM_TriPhysics"`), and may not rename, disguise, or
   re-wrap `.dnam` files into a proprietary file extension or container format
   to obscure their origin.
3. **Required Notices:** You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any
   part of the software from you (in source or binary form, including within
   product documentation or "About" notices of hardware devices and plugins)
   also gets a copy of these terms, as well as copies of any plain-text lines
   beginning with `Required Notice:` that the licensor provided with the
   software. For example:

> Required Notice: Copyright 2026 Peter Nguyen <peter@phn.dev>

