## Permitted Purposes & Anti-Resale Perimeter

Any commercial or noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose, **except** for:

1. **No Standalone Rebranded Resale or Hosted Cloning:** Selling, licensing for
   a fee, or offering to third parties as a hosted or managed cloud service a
   rebranded, white-labeled, or repackaged version of the project's standalone
   reference plugin (`packages/plugin`), differentiable trainer
   (`packages/trainer`), or web studio (`packages/web`) where the primary value
   of the product or service is substantially the software itself without
   substantial independent hardware or software functionality; or
2. **No Unbranded / White-Labeled Distribution:** Providing any hardware device,
   firmware, plugin, or software product that links, embeds, or uses
   `dnam-engine` or `.dnam` models while removing, obscuring, or replacing the
   mandatory **DNAM** branding required under [Mandatory DNAM Branding & Format
   Integrity](#mandatory-dnam-branding--format-integrity).

